      "answer": "1986",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "\" India is one of the parties of the Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD) treaty.  Prior to the CBD, India had different laws to govern the environment.  The Indian Wildlife Protection Act 1972 protected the biodiversity.  In addition to this act, the government passed the Environment (Protection) Act 1986 and Foreign Trade (Development and Regulation) Act 1992 for control of biodiversity.  === Renewable energy === Renewable energy in India comes under the purview of the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy.  India was the first country in the world to set up a ministry of non-conventional energy resources, in the early 1980s.  Its cumulative grid interactive or grid tied renewable energy capacity (excluding large hydro) has reached 203"
    },
