      "pubDate": "2026-06-27T15:51:19.431Z",
      "subject": "Environment & Ecology",
      "subSubject": "",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Elephants, the _____ and eight species of deer are also found",
      "answer": "Indian Rhinoceros",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Coniferous types are found in the northern high altitude regions and comprise pines, junipers and deodars.  There are 350 species of mammals, 375 reptiles, 130 amphibians, 20,000 insects, 19000 fish and 1200 species of birds in India.  The Asiatic lion, Bengal tiger and leopard are the main predators; the country has the most species of cats than any other.  Elephants, the Indian Rhinoceros and eight species of deer are also found.  There are over 17000 species of flowering plants in India, which account for six percent of the total plant species in the world.  India comprises seven percent of world's flora.  Wide range of climatic conditions in India gave rise to rich variety of flora"
    },
