      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Nayudu, their inaugural Test was against England at Lord's _____ from 25 to 28 June, but they were defeated by 158 runs",
      "answer": "Cricket Ground",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Not many records exist from the match.  The entire history of cricket in India and the sub-continent as a whole is based on the existence and development of the British Raj via the East India Company.  === 1918 to 1945 === India became the sixth national team to play Test cricket on their 1932 tour of England.  Nayudu, their inaugural Test was against England at Lord's Cricket Ground from 25 to 28 June, but they were defeated by 158 runs.  === 1945 to 1960 === The major and defining event in the history of Indian cricket during this period was the Partition of India following full independence from the British Raj in 1947.  An early casualty of change was the Bombay Quadrangular tournament, which had been a focal point of Indian cricket for over 50 years.  The new India had no place for teams based on ethnic origin"
    },
    {
      "id": "q138",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Sports",
      "region": "",
