      "question": "What is India's highest civilian award?",
      "answer": "Bharat Ratna",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Bharat Ratna (Sanskrit pronunciation: [bʱaːɾət̪ ɾət̪n̪(ᵊ)]; lit.  'Jewel of India') is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.  Instituted on 2 January 1954, the award is conferred in recognition of \"exceptional service/performance of the highest order\", without distinction of race, occupation, position or gender.  The award was originally limited to achievements in the arts, literature, science, and public services, but the Government of India expanded the criteria to include \"any field of human endeavor\" in December 2011"
    },
