      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Be engaged in innovation, development, or improvement of products or services.  == Issues == Startup India provides recognition to startups and unicorns.  The initiative was launched in 2016.  On January 16, 2026, the initiative marked its 10th anniversary, celebrating a decade of ecosystem growth.  As of December 2025, it reported that over 207,000 startups had been recognized across India, with approximately 50% emerging from tier-2 and tier-3 cities. By 2025, 112 unicorns are recognised including Paytm in 2018, Zomato in 2015 and Flipkart in 2012.  === Challenges === As of December 2025, over 2"
