      "subSubject": "Art & Culture",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____, the divorce rate is low — 1% compared with about 40% in the United States",
      "answer": "In India",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Historically, in most families the inheritance of family estates passed down the male line.  Since 1956, Indian laws treat males and females as equal in matters of inheritance without a legal will.  Indians are increasingly using a legal will for inheritance and property succession, with about 20 percent using a legal will by 2004.  In India, the divorce rate is low — 1% compared with about 40% in the United States.  These statistics do not reflect a complete picture, though.  There is a dearth of scientific surveys or studies on Indian marriages where the perspectives of both husbands and wives were solicited in-depth.  Sample surveys suggest the issues with marriages in India are similar to trends observed elsewhere in the world"
    },
    {
      "id": "q289",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
