      "question": "Several harvest festivals such as _____, Sohrai, Pusnâ, Hornbill, Chapchar Kut, Pongal, Onam and Raja sankaranti swinging festival are also fairly popular",
      "answer": "Makar Sankranti",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The three national holidays in India, the Independence Day, the Republic Day and the Gandhi Jayanti, are celebrated with zeal and enthusiasm across India.  In addition, many Indian states and regions have local festivals depending on prevalent religious and linguistic demographics.  Popular religious festivals include the Hindu festivals of Chhath, Navratri, Janmashtami, Diwali, Maha Shivratri, Ganesh Chaturthi, Durga Puja, Holi, Rath Yatra, Ugadi, Vasant Panchami, Rakshabandhan, and Dussehra.  Several harvest festivals such as Makar Sankranti, Sohrai, Pusnâ, Hornbill, Chapchar Kut, Pongal, Onam and Raja sankaranti swinging festival are also fairly popular.  India celebrates a variety of festivals due to the large diversity of India.  Many religious festivals like Diwali (Hindu) Eid (Muslim) Christmas (Christian), etc.  are celebrated by all"
    },
    {
      "id": "q296",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
      "region": "",
