      "fact": " Its trade with China has the largest deficit, about $31 billion in 2013.  India's reliance on external assistance and concessional debt has decreased since liberalisation of the economy, and the debt service ratio decreased from 35.  In India, external commercial borrowings (ECBs), or commercial loans from non-resident lenders, are being permitted by the government for providing an additional source of funds to Indian corporates.  The Ministry of Finance monitors and regulates them through ECB policy guidelines issued by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) under the Foreign Exchange Management Act of 1999.  India's foreign exchange reserves have steadily risen from $5. 8 billion in March 1991 to ₹38,832. 21 billion (US$540 billion) in July 2020"
