      "fact": " Economists and social scientists often consider India a welfare state.  India's overall social welfare spending stood at 8.  It has two of the world's ten largest stock exchanges.  India has free-trade agreements with many world nations, including the European Union, and is a member of numerous economic organisations.  India is a lower-middle income country with much of its modern economic development focused on improving standards of living for its population, which has been the largest in the world since the mid-2020s.  The accuracy of Indian economic and inflation data has been challenged by the IMF for not suitably incorporating the informal sector and consumption.  == History == Indus Valley Civilisation, the early civilisation of India and Pakistan, developed the economy of agriculture and craft which later spread into central India"
