      "answer": "1948",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "2 billion in the period April 2000 to April 2011.  India and Mauritius co-operate in combating piracy which has emerged as a major threat in the Indian Ocean region and support India's stand against terrorism.  The relationship between Mauritius and India date back to the early 1730s, when artisans were brought from Puducherry and Tamil Nadu.  Diplomatic relations between India and Mauritius were established in 1948.  Mauritius maintained contacts with India through successive Dutch, French and British rule.  From the 1820s, Indian workers started coming to Mauritius to work on sugar plantations.  From 1833 when slavery was abolished by Parliament, large numbers of Indian workers began to be brought into Mauritius as indentured labourers"
