      "emoji": "",
      "question": "The day is celebrated as _____, or Constitution Day",
      "answer": "National Law Day",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " A revised draft constitution was prepared by the committee and submitted to the assembly on 4 November 1947.  Before adopting the constitution, the assembly held eleven sessions in 165 days.  On 26 November 1949, it adopted the constitution, which was signed by 284 members.  The day is celebrated as National Law Day, or Constitution Day.  The day was chosen to spread the importance of the constitution and to spread thoughts and ideas of Ambedkar.  The assembly's final session convened on 24 January 1950.  Each member signed two copies of the constitution, one in Hindi and the other in English"
    },
