      "question": "In modern times, the Dehlavi dialect of the _____ became more prominent than Sanskrit",
      "answer": "Hindi Belt",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " His songs remain popular and are still widely sung in Bengal.  ==== Hindi literature ==== Hindi literature started as religious and philosophical poetry in medieval periods in dialects like Avadhi and Brij.  The most famous figures from this period are Kabir and Tulsidas.  In modern times, the Dehlavi dialect of the Hindi Belt became more prominent than Sanskrit.  ==== Gujarati literature ==== Gujarati literature's history may be traced to 1000 CE.  ==== Kannada literature ==== The oldest existing record of Kannada prose is the Halmidi inscription of 450 CE, and poetry in tripadi metre is the Kappe Arabhatta record of 700 CE.  The folk form of literature began earlier than any other literature in Kannada"
    },
