      "answer": "King Shivamara",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " ==== Gujarati literature ==== Gujarati literature's history may be traced to 1000 CE.  ==== Kannada literature ==== The oldest existing record of Kannada prose is the Halmidi inscription of 450 CE, and poetry in tripadi metre is the Kappe Arabhatta record of 700 CE.  The folk form of literature began earlier than any other literature in Kannada.  Gajashtaka (800 CE) by King Shivamara II, Chudamani (650 CE) by Thumbalacharya are examples of early literature now considered extinct.  Kavirajamarga by King Nripatunga Amoghavarsha I (850 CE) is the earliest existing literary work in Kannada.  It is a writing on literary criticism and poetics meant to standardise various written Kannada dialects used in literature in previous centuries.  The book makes reference to Kannada works by early writers such as King Durvinita of the 6th century and Ravikirti, the author of the Aihole record of 636 CE"
    },
