      "subject": "Indian History",
      "subSubject": "Indian History",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "of well-established, settled agricultural society is at Mehrgarh in the hills between the _____ and the Indus plain (today in Pakistan) (see Map 3",
      "answer": "Bolan Pass",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " According to Tim Dyson: \"By 7,000 years ago agriculture was firmly established in Baluchistan.  [and] slowly spread eastwards into the Indus valley. \" Michael Fisher adds: The earliest discovered instance .  of well-established, settled agricultural society is at Mehrgarh in the hills between the Bolan Pass and the Indus plain (today in Pakistan) (see Map 3.  From as early as 7000 BCE, communities there started investing increased labor in preparing the land and selecting, planting, tending, and harvesting particular grain-producing plants.  They also domesticated animals, including sheep, goats, pigs, and oxen (both humped zebu [Bos indicus] and unhumped [Bos taurus]).  Castrating oxen, for instance, turned them from mainly meat sources into domesticated draft-animals as well"
    },
