      "hint": "",
      "fact": " They formed a cultural bridge and played a vital role in trade as well as the transfer of ideas and culture to and from the Indo-Gangetic Plain to the southern tip of India.  They had to compete with the Shunga Empire and then the Kanva dynasty of Magadha to establish their rule.  Later, they played a crucial role to protect large part of India against foreign invaders like the Sakas, Yavanas and Pahlavas.  In particular, their struggles with the Western Kshatrapas went on for a long time.  The notable rulers of the Satavahana Dynasty Gautamiputra Satakarni and Sri Yajna Sātakarni were able to defeat the foreign invaders like the Western Kshatrapas and to stop their expansion.  In the 3rd century CE, the empire was split into smaller states.  ==== Trade and travels to India ==== The spice trade in Kerala attracted traders from all over the Old World to India"
