      "fact": " The Rashtrakuta rulers also patronised men of letters in a variety of languages.  === Gurjara-Pratihara Empire === The Gurjara-Pratiharas were instrumental in containing Arab armies moving east of the Indus River.  Nagabhata I defeated the Arab army under Junaid and Tamin during the Umayyad campaigns in India.  Under Nagabhata II, the Gurjara-Pratiharas became the most powerful dynasty in northern India.  He was succeeded by his son Ramabhadra, who ruled briefly before being succeeded by his son, Mihira Bhoja.  Under Bhoja and his successor Mahendrapala I, the Pratihara Empire reached its peak of prosperity and power.  By the time of Mahendrapala, its territory stretched from the border of Sindh in the west to Bihar in the east and from the Himalayas in the north to around the Narmada River in the south"
