      "question": "_____ easily routed the novice Mughal general",
      "answer": "Baji Rao",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Mughals suffered several blows due to invasions from Marathas, Rajputs, Jats and Afghans.  In 1737, the Maratha general Bajirao of the Maratha Empire invaded and plundered Delhi.  Under the general Amir Khan Umrao Al Udat, the Mughal Emperor sent 8,000 troops to drive away the 5,000 Maratha cavalry soldiers.  Baji Rao easily routed the novice Mughal general.  In 1737, in the final defeat of Mughal Empire, the commander-in-chief of the Mughal Army, Nizam-ul-mulk, was routed at Bhopal by the Maratha army.  This essentially brought an end to the Mughal Empire.  While Bharatpur State under Jat ruler Suraj Mal, overran the Mughal garrison at Agra and plundered the city"
    },
