      "answer": "After Kattabomman",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " He was captured by the British and hanged in 1799 CE.  Kattabomman refused to accept the sovereignty of East India Company, and fought against them.  Dheeran Chinnamalai was a Kongu Nadu chieftain and Palayakkarar from Tamil Nadu who fought against the East India Company.  After Kattabomman and Tipu Sultan's deaths, Chinnamalai sought the help of Marathas and Maruthu Pandiyar to attack the British at Coimbatore in 1800.  The British forces managed to stop the armies of the allies, forcing Chinnamalai to attack Coimbatore on his own.  His army was defeated and he escaped from the British forces.  Chinnamalai engaged in guerrilla warfare and defeated the British in battles at Cauvery in 1801, Odanilai in 1802 and Arachalur in 1804"
    },
