      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T12:59:21.328Z",
      "subject": "World History",
      "subSubject": "World History",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "The launch of Sputnik inaugurated the _____",
      "answer": "Space Race",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In August 1957, the Soviets successfully launched the world's first intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM), and in October they launched the first Earth satellite, Sputnik 1.  This led to what became known as the Sputnik crisis.  The Central Intelligence Agency described the orbit of Sputnik 1 as a \"stupendous scientific achievement\" and concluded that the USSR had likely perfected an intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) capable of reaching 'any desired target with accuracy'.  The launch of Sputnik inaugurated the Space Race.  This led to a series of historic space exploration milestones, and most notably the Apollo Moon landings from 1969 by the United States, which astronaut Frank Borman later described as \"just a battle in the Cold War. \" The public's reaction in the Soviet Union was mixed.  The Soviet government limited the release of information about the lunar landing, which affected the reaction"
    },
