      "fact": " In addition, the security advantage of a buffer zone was recognized as irrelevant and the Soviets officially declared that they would no longer intervene in the affairs of satellite states in Central and Eastern Europe.  Bush and Gorbachev met at the Moscow Summit in May 1988 and the Governors Island Summit in December 1988.  In 1989, Soviet forces withdrew from Afghanistan without achieving their objectives.  Later that year, the Berlin Wall, the Inner German border and the Iron Curtain fell.  On 3 December 1989, Gorbachev and Bush declared the Cold War over at the Malta Summit.  In February 1990, Gorbachev agreed with the US-proposed Treaty on the Final Settlement with Respect to Germany and signed it on 12 September 1990, paving the way for the German reunification.  When the Berlin Wall came down, Gorbachev's \"Common European Home\" concept began to take shape"
