      "question": "_____'s son, Satyajit Padhye is also a ventriloquist and puppeteer",
      "answer": "Ramdas Padhye",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Kathputli, a form of string puppet performance native to Rajasthan, is notable and there are many Indian ventriloquists and puppeteers.  The first Indian ventriloquist, Professor Y.  Padhye, introduced this form of puppetry to India in the 1920s and his son, Ramdas Padhye, subsequently popularised ventriloquism and puppetry.  Ramdas Padhye's son, Satyajit Padhye is also a ventriloquist and puppeteer.  Almost all types of puppets are found in India.  String puppets India has a rich and ancient tradition of string puppets or marionettes.  Marionettes with jointed limbs controlled by strings allow far greater flexibility and are therefore the most articulate of the puppets"
    },
    {
      "id": "q1769",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T12:59:32.443Z",
      "subject": "Art & Culture",
      "subSubject": "Art & Culture",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Rajasthan, Orissa, Karnataka and _____ are some of the regions where this form of puppetry has flourished",
      "answer": "Tamil Nadu",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Almost all types of puppets are found in India.  String puppets India has a rich and ancient tradition of string puppets or marionettes.  Marionettes with jointed limbs controlled by strings allow far greater flexibility and are therefore the most articulate of the puppets.  Rajasthan, Orissa, Karnataka and Tamil Nadu are some of the regions where this form of puppetry has flourished.  The traditional marionettes of Rajasthan are known as Kathputli.  Carved from a single piece of wood, these puppets are like large dolls that are colorfully dressed.  The string puppets of Orissa are known as Kundhei"
    },
    {
      "id": "q1770",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T12:59:32.444Z",
      "subject": "Art & Culture",
      "subSubject": "Art & Culture",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Puppets from _____, known as Bommalattam, combine the techniques of rod and string puppets",
      "answer": "Tamil Nadu",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Carved from a single piece of wood, these puppets are like large dolls that are colorfully dressed.  The string puppets of Orissa are known as Kundhei.  The string puppets of Karnataka are called Gombeyatta.  Puppets from Tamil Nadu, known as Bommalattam, combine the techniques of rod and string puppets.  Rod puppets Rod puppets are an extension of glove-puppets but are often much larger and supported and manipulated by rods from below.  This form of puppetry now is found mostly in West Bengal and Orissa.  The traditional rod puppet form of West Bengal is known as Putul Nautch"
    },
