      "fact": " Most early and medieval art in India is Hindu, Buddhist or Jain.  A freshly made coloured floor design (Rangoli) is still a common sight outside the doorstep of many (mostly South Indian) Indian homes.  Raja Ravi Varma is one of the classical painters from medieval India.  Pattachitra, Madhubani painting, Mysore painting, Rajput painting, Tanjore painting and Mughal painting are some notable Genres of Indian Art; while Nandalal Bose, M.  Raza, Geeta Vadhera, Jamini Roy and B.  Venkatappa are some modern painters.  Among the present-day artists, Atul Dodiya, Bose Krishnamacnahri, Devajyoti Ray and Shibu Natesan represent a new era of Indian art where global art shows direct amalgamation with Indian classical styles"
