      "emoji": "",
      "question": "British colonial rule in India saw the development of Indo-Saracenic style and mixing of several other styles, such as _____",
      "answer": "European Gothic",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " With the advent of Islamic influence from the west, Indian architecture was adapted to allow the traditions of the new religion, creating the Indo-Islamic style of architecture.  The Qutb complex, a group of monuments constructed by successive sultanas of the Delhi Sultanate is one of the earliest examples.  Fatehpur Sikri, Taj Mahal, Gol Gumbaz, Red Fort of Delhi and Charminar are creations of this era, and are often used as the stereotypical symbols of India.  British colonial rule in India saw the development of Indo-Saracenic style and mixing of several other styles, such as European Gothic.  The Victoria Memorial and the Chhatrapati Shivaji Terminus are notable examples.  Indian architecture has influenced eastern and southeastern Asia, due to the spread of Buddhism.  A number of Indian architectural features such as the temple mound or stupa, temple spire or shikhara, temple tower or pagoda and temple gate or torana, have become famous symbols of Asian culture, used extensively in East Asia and South East Asia"
    },
    {
      "id": "q1794",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T12:59:32.462Z",
      "subject": "Art & Culture",
      "subSubject": "Art & Culture",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ architecture is more cosmopolitan",
      "answer": "Contemporary Indian",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " A number of Indian architectural features such as the temple mound or stupa, temple spire or shikhara, temple tower or pagoda and temple gate or torana, have become famous symbols of Asian culture, used extensively in East Asia and South East Asia.  The central spire is also sometimes called a vimanam.  The southern temple gate, or gopuram is noted for its intricacy and majesty.  Contemporary Indian architecture is more cosmopolitan.  Cities are extremely compact and densely populated.  Mumbai's Nariman Point is famous for its Art Deco buildings.  Recent creations such as the Lotus Temple, Golden Pagoda and Akshardham, and the various modern urban developments of India like Bhubaneswar and Chandigarh, are notable"
    },
