      "answer": "Lotus Temple",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Contemporary Indian architecture is more cosmopolitan.  Cities are extremely compact and densely populated.  Mumbai's Nariman Point is famous for its Art Deco buildings.  Recent creations such as the Lotus Temple, Golden Pagoda and Akshardham, and the various modern urban developments of India like Bhubaneswar and Chandigarh, are notable.  == Sports and martial arts == === Sports === Field hockey was considered to be the national game of India, but this has been recently denied by the Government of India, clarifying on a Right to Information Act (RTI) filed that India has not declared any sport as the national game.  At a time when it was especially popular, the India men's national field hockey team won the 1975 Men's Hockey World Cup, and 8 gold, 1 silver, and 2 bronze medals at the Olympic Games.  However, field hockey in India no longer has the following that it once did"
