      "answer": "Ram Gopal Varma",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The total output of Indian cinema, taking into account all the languages, is the largest in the world in terms of number of films produced and number of tickets sold.  India has produced many cinema-makers like S. Rajamouli, Satyajit Ray, Mrinal Sen, J.  Viswanath, Ram Gopal Varma, Bapu, Ritwik Ghatak, Guru Dutt, Adoor Gopalakrishnan, Shaji N.  Karun, Girish Kasaravalli, Shekhar Kapoor, Hrishikesh Mukherjee, Nagraj Manjule, Shyam Benegal, Shankar Nag, Girish Karnad, G.  Iyer, Mani Ratnam, and K.  Balachander (see also: Indian film directors)"
