      "fact": " The governments loosened restrictions on business creation and import controls while also promoting the growth of the automobile, digitalization, telecommunications and software industries.  Reforms under lead to an increase in the average GDP growth rate from 2. 9 percent in the 1970s to 5. 6 per cent, although they failed to fix systemic issues with the Licence Raj.  Despite Rajiv Gandhi's dream for more systemic reforms, the Bofors scandal tarnished his government's reputation and impeded his liberalisation efforts.  Growth during the 1980s was higher than in the preceding decades but fragile.  It not only culminated in a crisis in June 1991 but also exhibited significantly higher variance than growth in the 1990s"
