      "question": "It represents the southernmost part of the Indian peninsula, situated south of the stable _____",
      "answer": "Dharwar Craton",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Vast reserves of metal ores and coal have been found in the Chota Nagpur plateau.  Southern Garanulite terrain: Covers South India especially Tamil Nadu excluding western and eastern ghats.  The Southern Granulite Terrain (SGT) is one of the most geologically significant regions of the Indian Shield.  It represents the southernmost part of the Indian peninsula, situated south of the stable Dharwar Craton. Unlike the lower-grade metamorphic rocks found further north, the SGT is composed of high-grade metamorphic rocks (granulites) that were formed deep within the Earth's crust under extreme pressure and temperature.  Northern Boundary: It is separated from the Dharwar Craton by a transition zone often referred to as the \"Fermor Line. \" Major Shear Zones: These act as the \"boundaries\" between different blocks within the SGT: Moyar-Bhavani Shear Zone: Separates the Dharwar Craton from the Nilgiri Block"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2195",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Geography",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:00:36.938Z",
      "subject": "Geography",
      "subSubject": "Geography",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____: It is separated from the Dharwar Craton by a transition zone often referred to as the \"Fermor Line",
      "answer": "Northern Boundary",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Southern Granulite Terrain (SGT) is one of the most geologically significant regions of the Indian Shield.  It represents the southernmost part of the Indian peninsula, situated south of the stable Dharwar Craton. Unlike the lower-grade metamorphic rocks found further north, the SGT is composed of high-grade metamorphic rocks (granulites) that were formed deep within the Earth's crust under extreme pressure and temperature.  Northern Boundary: It is separated from the Dharwar Craton by a transition zone often referred to as the \"Fermor Line. \" Major Shear Zones: These act as the \"boundaries\" between different blocks within the SGT: Moyar-Bhavani Shear Zone: Separates the Dharwar Craton from the Nilgiri Block.  Palghat-Cauvery Shear Zone (PCSZ): A massive tectonic boundary that many geologists consider the \"suture\" where different ancient landmasses joined.  Achankovil Shear Zone (ASZ): Located further south, separating the Madurai Block from the Trivandrum Block"
    },
    {
