      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Northern Boundary: It is separated from the Dharwar Craton by a transition zone often referred to as the \"Fermor Line. \" Major Shear Zones: These act as the \"boundaries\" between different blocks within the SGT: Moyar-Bhavani Shear Zone: Separates the Dharwar Craton from the Nilgiri Block.  Palghat-Cauvery Shear Zone (PCSZ): A massive tectonic boundary that many geologists consider the \"suture\" where different ancient landmasses joined.  Achankovil Shear Zone (ASZ): Located further south, separating the Madurai Block from the Trivandrum Block.  Deccan Plateau, also called Deccan Trapps, is a large triangular plateau, bounded by the Vindhyas to the north and flanked by the Eastern and Western Ghats.  The Deccan covers a total area of 1. 9 million km2 (730,000 sq mi)"
