      "hint": "",
      "fact": " During the monsoons, the area turn into a shallow marsh, often flooding to knee-depth.  After the monsoons, the region turns dry and becomes parched.  ==== Arable land ==== India's arable land area of 1,597,000 km2 (394. 6 million acres) is the second largest in the world, after the United States.  Its gross irrigated crop area of 826,000 km2 (215. 6 million acres) is the largest in the world, followed by US and China.  Of the 160 million hectares of cultivated land in India, about 39 million hectare can be irrigated by groundwater wells and an additional 22 million hectares by irrigation canals"
