      "answer": "Arunachal Pradesh",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Trap soil is black in colour and conducive to agriculture.  The Carboniferous system, Permian System and Triassic systems are seen in the western Himalayas.  The Jurassic system is seen in the western Himalayas and Rajasthan.  Tertiary imprints are seen in parts of Manipur, Nagaland, Arunachal Pradesh and along the Himalayan belt.  The Cretaceous system is seen in central India in the Vindhyas and part of the Indo-Gangetic plains.  The Gondwana system is seen in the Narmada River area in the Vindhyas and Satpuras.  The Eocene system is seen in the western Himalayas and Assam"
    },
