      "answer": "In June",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Based on observations, heat wave related mortality has increased in India prior to 2005.  The 2015 Indian heat wave killed more than 2,500 people.  In April 2024, the India Meteorological Department (IMD) forecasted a heat wave spell lasting approximately ten to twenty days longer than normal length of four to eight days during the three-month period between April and June.  In June 2024, day temperatures reached 44. 8 °F) in New Delhi, which were at their highest in six years.  Five people have been reported dead due to this heatwave.  In India as a whole, heat exposure in 2024 resulted in an estimated loss of 247 billion potential labour hours, representing a 124% increase compared with the average recorded during the 1990s"
