      "answer": "During World War",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Maratha Kanhoji Angre, and Kunjali Marakkar, the Naval chief of Saamoothiri were two notable naval chiefs of the period.  === British India (1857 to 1947) === The Royal Indian Navy was first established by the British while much of India was under the control of the East India Company.  In 1892, it became a maritime component as the Royal Indian Marine (RIM).  During World War I, the Indian Army contributed several divisions and independent brigades to the European, Mediterranean, and Middle Eastern theatres of war.  One million Indian troops served overseas; 62,000 died, and another 67,000 were wounded.  In total, 74,187 Indian soldiers died during the war.  It fought against the German Empire in German East Africa and on the Western Front"
