      "answer": "German Empire",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " During World War I, the Indian Army contributed several divisions and independent brigades to the European, Mediterranean, and Middle Eastern theatres of war.  One million Indian troops served overseas; 62,000 died, and another 67,000 were wounded.  In total, 74,187 Indian soldiers died during the war.  It fought against the German Empire in German East Africa and on the Western Front.  Indian divisions were also sent to Egypt, Gallipoli, and nearly 700,000 served in Mesopotamia against the Ottoman Empire.  Following WWI, the Indian Armed Forces underwent a significant transformation.  In 1928, Engineer Sub-lieutenant D"
