      "answer": "Ottoman Empire",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " One million Indian troops served overseas; 62,000 died, and another 67,000 were wounded.  In total, 74,187 Indian soldiers died during the war.  It fought against the German Empire in German East Africa and on the Western Front.  Indian divisions were also sent to Egypt, Gallipoli, and nearly 700,000 served in Mesopotamia against the Ottoman Empire.  Following WWI, the Indian Armed Forces underwent a significant transformation.  In 1928, Engineer Sub-lieutenant D.  Mukherji became the first Indian to receive a commission in the Royal Indian Marine"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2394",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Defence",
