      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Each command is headed by an air officer commanding-in-chief with the rank of air marshal.  There are two joint commands whose head can belong to any of the three services.  These are the Strategic Forces Command and the Andaman and Nicobar Command.  Apart from these, there is an Integrated Defence Staff.  The lack of an overall military commander has helped keep the Indian Armed Forces under civilian control and has prevented the rise of military dictatorships unlike in neighboring Pakistan.  The Armed Forces have four main tasks: To assert the territorial integrity of India.  To defend the country if attacked by a foreign nation"
