      "answer": "Param Vir Chakra",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "3 million paramilitary personnel, making it one of the world's largest military forces.  A total of 1,567,390 ex- servicemen are registered with the Indian Army, the majority of them hailing from: Uttar Pradesh (271,928), Punjab (191,702), Haryana (165,702), Maharashtra (143,951), Kerala (127,920), Tamil Nadu (103,156), Rajasthan (100,592) and Himachal Pradesh (78,321).  Many of them are re-employed in various Central government sectors.  The highest wartime gallantry award given by the Military of India is the Param Vir Chakra (PVC), followed by the Maha Vir Chakra (MVC) and the Vir Chakra (VrC).  Their peacetime equivalents are Ashoka Chakra Award, Kirti Charka, and Shaurya Chakra respectively.  The highest decoration for meritorious service is the Param Vishisht Seva Medal (PVSM), followed by Ati Vishisht Seva Medal (AVSM) and Vishisht Seva Medal (VSM).  Awards for distinguished services rendered in wartime and hostilities are Uttam Yudh Seva Medal (UYSM) and Yudh Seva Medal (YSM)"
    },
