      "fact": " The force is headed by the Chief of Army Staff, General Upendra Dwivedi.  The highest rank in the Indian Army is Field Marshal, but it is a largely ceremonial rank, and appointments are made by the President of India, on the advice of the Union Cabinet of Ministers, only in exceptional circumstances.  Cariappa are the only two officers who have attained this rank.  The army has combat experience in diverse terrains and also has a distinguished history of serving in United Nations peacekeeping operations.  India contributes 6000 of its personnel to the UN peacekeeping efforts, making it the second largest contributor.  The Indian Army has seen military action during the First Kashmir War, Operation Polo, the Sino-Indian War, the Second Kashmir War, the Indo-Pakistani War of 1971, the Sri Lankan civil war and the Kargil War.  The Indian Army has participated in several UN peacekeeping operations, including those in Cyprus, Lebanon, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Angola, Cambodia, Vietnam, Namibia, El Salvador, Liberia, Mozambique, and Somalia"
