      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Indian Air Force plays a crucial role in securing Indian airspace and also in India's power projection in South Asia and the Indian Ocean.  Therefore, modernising and expanding the Indian Air Force is a top priority for the Indian government.  Over the years, the IAF has grown from a tactical force to one with transoceanic reach.  The strategic reach emerges from the induction of Force Multipliers like Flight Refuelling Aircraft (FRA), Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV), and credible strategic lift capabilities.  === Aircraft === Historically, the IAF has generally relied on Soviet, British, Israeli, and French military craft and technology to support its growth.  IAF's primary air superiority fighter with the additional capability to conduct air-ground (strike) missions is Sukhoi Su-30MKI.  The IAF has placed an order for a total of 272 Su-30MKIs, of which 205 are in service as of May 2015"
