      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:01:27.070Z",
      "subject": "Defence",
      "subSubject": "Defence",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ team also successfully scaled Everest from the north face, the more technically challenging route",
      "answer": "Another Navy",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === Indian Navy exploration === The Indian Navy regularly conducts adventure expeditions.  The sailing ship and training vessel INS Tarangini began circumnavigating the world on 23 January 2003, intending to foster good relations with other nations; she returned to India in May of the following year after visiting 36 ports in 18 nations.  Kohli led the Indian Navy's first successful expedition to Mount Everest in 1965.  Another Navy team also successfully scaled Everest from the north face, the more technically challenging route.  An Indian Navy team comprising 11 members completed an expedition to the North Pole in 2006.  The Indian Naval ensign first flew in Antarctica in 1981.  The Indian Navy succeeded in Mission Dakshin Dhruv by traversing to the South Pole on skis in 2006"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2567",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Defence",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:01:27.071Z",
      "subject": "Defence",
      "subSubject": "Defence",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ team comprising 11 members completed an expedition to the North Pole in 2006",
      "answer": "An Indian Navy",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The sailing ship and training vessel INS Tarangini began circumnavigating the world on 23 January 2003, intending to foster good relations with other nations; she returned to India in May of the following year after visiting 36 ports in 18 nations.  Kohli led the Indian Navy's first successful expedition to Mount Everest in 1965.  Another Navy team also successfully scaled Everest from the north face, the more technically challenging route.  An Indian Navy team comprising 11 members completed an expedition to the North Pole in 2006.  The Indian Naval ensign first flew in Antarctica in 1981.  The Indian Navy succeeded in Mission Dakshin Dhruv by traversing to the South Pole on skis in 2006.  With this historic expedition, they set the record for being the world's first military team to have completed a ski traverse to the geographic south pole"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2568",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Defence",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:01:27.073Z",
      "subject": "Defence",
      "subSubject": "Defence",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "To remove such confusion, in 2011 the Ministry of _____ adopted the uniform nomenclature of Central Armed Police Forces for only five of its Primary Police organisations",
      "answer": "Home Affairs",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": ", Army, Navy, and Air Force.  Further the Supreme Court of India in a case reported in AIR 2000 SC 3948 clarified that unless it is a service in the three principal wing of the Armed Forces, a force included in the expression \"Armed forces of the Union\" does not constitute part of the military service/military.  To differentiate from Armed Forces, Some of other forces were commonly referred to as Central Paramilitary Forces which caused confusion and give the impression of them being part of the military forces.  To remove such confusion, in 2011 the Ministry of Home Affairs adopted the uniform nomenclature of Central Armed Police Forces for only five of its Primary Police organisations.  These were formerly called as Paramilitary Forces.  Central Armed Police Forces are still incorrectly referred to as \"Paramilitary Forces\" in the media and in some correspondence.  These forces are headed by officers from the Indian Police Service and are under the Ministry of Home Affairs"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2569",
