      "question": "What is Maritime service branch of the Indian Armed Forces?",
      "answer": "Indian Navy",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Indian Navy (IN) (ISO: Bhāratīya Nau Senā) is the maritime branch of the Indian Armed Forces.  The President of India is the Supreme Commander of the Indian Navy.  The Chief of Naval Staff, a four-star admiral, commands the navy.  As a blue-water navy, it operates significantly in the Persian Gulf Region, the Horn of Africa, the Strait of Malacca, and routinely conducts anti-piracy operations with other navies in the region"
    },
