      "fact": " ==== Permanent commission ==== To be eligible for the National Defence Academy and Naval Academy Examination, the candidates must have taken Physics and Mathematics at their 10+2 level.  Additionally, the candidates are required to be physically fit and sound, along with no medical ailments.  Through the NDA/NA examination, candidates, the navy offers two streams to candidates — NDA Navy and INA (4-year) program.  Candidates opting for the NDA Navy course go through training at National Defence Academy for three years, along with NDA Army and Air Force cadets.  Afterwards, the candidates are moved to Indian Naval Academy for specialised training in naval warfare, maritime law, naval operations, gunnery, etc.  After the successful completion of training, the candidates are awarded a B. Sc degree and are commissioned as Sub-Lieutenants in general executive branch"
