      "question": "_____ team also successfully scaled Everest from the north face, a technically more challenging route",
      "answer": "Another Navy",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === Exploration === The Indian Navy regularly conducts adventure expeditions.  The sailing ship and training vessel INS Tarangini began circumnavigating the world on 23 January 2003, intending to foster good relations with various other nations; she returned to India in May 2004 after visiting 36 ports in 18 nations.  Kohli led the Indian Navy's first successful expedition to Mount Everest in 1965; the Navy's ensign was again flown atop Everest on 19 May 2004 by a similar expedition.  Another Navy team also successfully scaled Everest from the north face, a technically more challenging route.  The expedition was led by Cdr Satyabrata Dam of the submarine arm.  Dam is a mountaineer of international repute and has climbed many mountains including the Patagonias, the Alps among others.  In 2017, to commemorate 50 years of the Navy's first expedition in 1965, a team set off to climb Mount Everest"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2901",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Defence",
