      "fact": " Also, three of the ten member team—the expedition leader—Cdr.  Satyabrata Dam, leading medical assistants Rakesh Kumar and Vikas Kumar are now among the few people in the world to have visited the two poles and summited Mount Everest.  Indian Navy became the first organisation to reach the poles and Mount Everest.  Dilip Donde completed the first solo circumnavigation by an Indian citizen on 22 May 2010.  Abhilash Tomy became the first Indian to complete a solo, non-stop circumnavigation of the world on a sailboat not fitted with any technology or navigational aids.  Navika Sagar Parikrama (lit.  'Sailors' Sea Circumambulation') was a circumnavigation of the globe by female officers of the Indian Navy"
    },
