      "fact": " The high temperatures are expected to affect 23 states in 2019, up from nine in 2015 and 19 in 2018.  The number of heat wave days has increased—not just day temperature, night temperatures increased also.  2018 was the country's sixth hottest year on record, and 11 of its 15 warmest years have occurred since 2004.  In 2024, the capital New Delhi recorded the country's hottest-ever temperature 49.  In response, New Delhi authorities warned citizens of water shortages, cutting supplies in some areas.  The water prime minister, Atishi Marlena, called for \"collective responsibility\" to deal with water scarcity and reduced water supply from twice a day to once a day in some areas.  Also in 2024, the heat waves caused problems for India's elections, when 33 poll workers died from extreme heat"
    },
