      "question": "Under the new visa agreement signed during the Argentine Presidential visit in October _____, it has been agreed that five-year multi-entry business visas would be given free of co",
      "answer": "2009",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India has an embassy in Buenos Aires and Argentina has an embassy in New Delhi.  As of January 2025, the Indian Ambassador to Argentina (concurrently accredited to Uruguay and Paraguay) is Shri Ajaneesh Kumar.  According to the Ministry of External Affairs of the Government of India, \"Under the 1968 Visa agreement, (Argentine) fees for transit and tourist visas have been abolished.  Under the new visa agreement signed during the Argentine Presidential visit in October 2009, it has been agreed that five-year multi-entry business visas would be given free of cost.  The Embassy of India in Buenos Aires gives Cafe Con Visa (coffee with visa) to Argentine visitors.  The applicants are invited for coffee and a visa is given immediately.  This has been praised by the Argentine media, public and the Foreign Minister himself"
