      "question": "However, India has enjoyed a favourable relationship with Bangladesh during governments formed by the Awami League in _____ and 1996",
      "answer": "1972",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Bangladesh India was the second country to recognise Bangladesh as a separate and independent state, doing so on 6 December 1971.  India fought alongside the Bangladeshis to liberate Bangladesh from West Pakistan in 1971.  Bangladesh's relationship with India has been difficult in terms of border killing, irrigation and land border disputes post-1976.  However, India has enjoyed a favourable relationship with Bangladesh during governments formed by the Awami League in 1972 and 1996.  The recent solutions to land and maritime disputes have taken out irritants in ties.  At the outset, India's relations with Bangladesh could not have been stronger because of India's unalloyed support for independence and opposition against Pakistan in 1971.  During the independence war, many refugees fled to India"
