      "question": "In _____, a Free Trade Agreement was signed between the two countries",
      "answer": "2003",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Both countries are members of BIMSTEC.  Indian prime minister Rajiv Gandhi, P.  Narasimha Rao, Atal Bihari Vajpayee, and Manmohan Singh, have visited Thailand, which was reciprocated by contemporary Thai Prime Ministers Chatichai Choonhavan, Thaksin Sinawatra, and Surayud Chulanont.  In 2003, a Free Trade Agreement was signed between the two countries.  India is the 13th largest investor in Thailand.  The spheres of trade are in chemicals, pharmaceuticals, textiles, nylon, tyre cord, real estate, rayon fibres, paper-grade pulps, steel wires, and rods.  However, IT services, and manufacturing, are the main spheres"
