      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Indian Foreign Secretary is the head of the Indian Foreign Service (IFS) and therefore, serves as the head of all Indian (ambassadors) and high commissioners.  Vinay Mohan Kwatra is the current Foreign Secretary of India.  === Act East Policy === In the post-Cold War era, a significant aspect of India's foreign policy is the Look East Policy.  During the cold war, India's relations with its Southeast Asian neighbours were not strong.  After the end of the cold war, the government of India particularly realised the importance of redressing this imbalance in India's foreign policy.  Consequently, the Narsimha Rao government in the early 1990s unveiled the look east policy.  Initially, it focused on renewing political and economic contacts with the countries of East and South-East Asia"
