      "answer": "Egypt Both",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India has been a partner in Ethiopia's developmental efforts, training Ethiopian personnel under its ITEC programmer, providing it with several lines of credit and launching the Pan-African e-Network project there in 2007.  The Second India–Africa Forum Summit was held in Addis Ababa in 2011.  India is also Ethiopia's second-largest source of foreign direct investments.  Egypt Both countries established diplomatic relations on 18 August 1947.  Modern Egypt-India relations go back to the contacts between Saad Zaghloul and Mohandas Gandhi on the common goals of their respective movements of independence.  In 1955, Egypt under Gamal Abdul Nasser and India under Jawaharlal Nehru became the founders of the Non-Aligned Movement.  During the 1956 War, Nehru stood supporting Egypt to the point of threatening to withdraw his country from the Commonwealth of Nations"
