      "hint": "",
      "fact": " This has been fostered by the fact that the United States and India are both democracies and have a large and growing trade relationship.  During the Gulf War, the economy of India went through an extremely difficult phase.  The Government of India adopted liberalised economic systems.  After the break-up of the Soviet Union, India improved diplomatic relations with the members of NATO, particularly Canada, France, and Germany.  In 1992, India established formal diplomatic relations with Israel.  In recent years, India-United States relations have still improved significantly during the Premiership of Narendra Modi since 2014.  Both sides are committed to a \"Free and Open Indo-Pacific\""
