      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ furnished relief and reconstruction aid",
      "answer": "Afterwards India",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " At the outset, India's relations with Bangladesh could not have been stronger because of India's unalloyed support for independence and opposition against Pakistan in 1971.  During the independence war, many refugees fled to India.  When the struggle of resistance matured in November 1971, India also intervened militarily and may have helped bring international attention to the issue through Indira Gandhi's visit to Washington, D.  Afterwards India furnished relief and reconstruction aid.  India extended recognition to Bangladesh before the end of the war in 1971 (the second country to do so after Bhutan) and subsequently lobbied others to follow suit.  India also withdrew its military from the land of Bangladesh when Sheikh Mujibur Rahman requested Indira Gandhi to do so during the latter's visit to Dhaka in 1972.  Indo-Bangladesh relations have been somewhat less friendly since the fall of the Mujib government in August 1975"
    },
    {
      "id": "q3331",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "International Relations",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:02:20.921Z",
      "subject": "International Relations",
      "subSubject": "International Relations",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "India also withdrew its military from the land of Bangladesh when _____ requested Indira Gandhi to do so during the latter's visit to Dhaka in 1972",
      "answer": "Sheikh Mujibur Rahman",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " When the struggle of resistance matured in November 1971, India also intervened militarily and may have helped bring international attention to the issue through Indira Gandhi's visit to Washington, D.  Afterwards India furnished relief and reconstruction aid.  India extended recognition to Bangladesh before the end of the war in 1971 (the second country to do so after Bhutan) and subsequently lobbied others to follow suit.  India also withdrew its military from the land of Bangladesh when Sheikh Mujibur Rahman requested Indira Gandhi to do so during the latter's visit to Dhaka in 1972.  Indo-Bangladesh relations have been somewhat less friendly since the fall of the Mujib government in August 1975.  over the years over issues such as South Talpatti Island, the Tin Bigha Corridor and access to Nepal, the Farakka Barrage and water sharing, border conflicts near Tripura and the construction of a fence along most of the border which India explains as security provision against migrants, insurgents and terrorists.  Many Bangladeshis feel India likes to play \"big brother\" to smaller neighbours, including Bangladesh"
    },
