      "answer": "Through Buddhism",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India is the 13th largest investor in Thailand.  The spheres of trade are in chemicals, pharmaceuticals, textiles, nylon, tyre cord, real estate, rayon fibres, paper-grade pulps, steel wires, and rods.  However, IT services, and manufacturing, are the main spheres.  Through Buddhism, India has culturally influenced Thailand.  The Indian epics, Mahabharata, and Ramayana, are popular and are widely taught in schools as part of the curriculum in Thailand.  The example can also be seen in temples around Thailand, where the story of Ramayana and renowned Indian folk stories are depicted on the temple wall.  Thailand has become a big tourist destination for Indians"
