      "fact": " The dispute intensified in 1997 as the Nepali parliament considered a treaty on the hydroelectric development of the river.  India and Nepal differ as to which stream constitutes the source of the river.  Nepal regards the Limpiyadhura as the source; India claims the Lipu Lekh.  Nepal has reportedly tabled an 1856 map from the British India Office to support its position.  The countries have held several meetings about the dispute and discussed jointly surveying to resolve the issue.  Although the Indo-Nepali dispute appears to be minor, it was aggravated in 1962 by tensions between China and India.  Because the disputed area lies near the Sino-Indian frontier, it gains strategic value"
