      "question": "_____'s Day 1942, Roosevelt, Churchill, the Soviet Union's former Foreign Minister Maxim Litvinov, and the Chinese Premier T",
      "answer": "On New Year",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " It incorporated Soviet suggestions but included no role for France.  One major change from the Atlantic Charter was the addition of a provision for religious freedom, which Stalin approved after Roosevelt insisted.  Roosevelt's idea of the \"Four Powers,\" refers to the four major Allied countries, the United States, the United Kingdom, the Soviet Union, and China, emerged in the Declaration by the United Nations.  On New Year's Day 1942, Roosevelt, Churchill, the Soviet Union's former Foreign Minister Maxim Litvinov, and the Chinese Premier T.  Soong signed the \"Declaration by United Nations,\" and the next day the representatives of twenty-two other nations added their signatures.  During the war, the United Nations became the official term for the Allies.  In order to join, countries had to sign the Declaration and declare war on the Axis powers"
