      "answer": "In January",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Other countries began to follow suit, triggering a financial crisis.  On 19 May 2025, only 61 countries paid their dues on time and in full.  The crisis is causing massive budget cuts within the UN, with the UN warning that millions of lives are being put at risk.  In January 2026, Guterres sent a letter to all members about an \"imminent financial collapse\" of the UN.  == Structure == The United Nations is part of the broader UN System, which includes an extensive network of institutions and entities.  Central to the organization are five principal organs established by the UN Charter: the General Assembly, the Security Council, the Economic and Social Council, the International Court of Justice and the UN Secretariat.  A sixth principal organ, the Trusteeship Council, suspended its operations on 1 November 1994 upon the independence of Palau; the last remaining UN trustee territory"
