      "fact": " Every child between the age of 6 to 14 years is entitled to free education.  In the case of Kesavananda Bharati v.  State of Kerala (1973)[1], it was held by the Supreme Court that Fundamental Rights can be amended by the Parliament, however, such amendment should not contravene the basic structure of the Constitution.  == Origins == The first demand for fundamental rights came in the form of the \"Constitution of India Bill, in 1895.  Also popularly known as the Swaraj Bill 1895, it was written during the emergence of Indian nationalism and increasingly vocal demands by Indians for self-government.  It talked about freedom of speech, right to privacy, right to franchise, etc.  In the following period, attempts were made from quarters asking the British government to grant rights for Indians"
