      "question": "What is National court system?",
      "answer": "Judiciary of India",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Judiciary of India (ISO: Bhārata kī Nyāyapālikā) is the system of courts that interpret and apply the law in the Republic of India.  The Constitution of India provides concept for a single and unified judiciary in India.  India uses a mixed legal system based majorly on the common law with civil laws applicable in certain territories in combination with certain religion specific personal laws.  The judiciary is made in three levels with subsidiary parts"
    },
    {
      "id": "q3799",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Constitution",
      "region": "",
