      "answer": "District Judge",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " It recommended raising the salaries of the district judiciary and fixed their overall compensation.  Ten years later, the second NJPC was headed by P.  === Position and designation held by Judges (in hierarchy) in their career and pay scale === === Career progression === A judicial officer typically begins his or her career as a civil judge in a Court of Judicial Magistrate of First Class (JMFC).  After seven years of experience judges can be appointed to the post of District Judge via a competitive examination.  The retirement age for the judicial officers is 60 years in the District court, 62 years in the High Courts, and 65 in the Supreme Court.  All officers belonging to the Judicial Services, from entry-level to topmost position, falls under Group-A (Gazetted) Service.  Entry-level positions in the Courts of Judicial Magistrate of First Class are generally considered probationary, or training posts"
