      "question": "=== 21st century === _____ was one of the key members during 1989–2013 for Team India in multiple formats",
      "answer": "Sachin Tendulkar",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In addition to its spread through television, its globalization has a direct link to India's increase in consumerism.  As the sport became increasingly popular in India in the 1980s into and 1990s, India experienced a rapid expansion of both televised and billboard advertising.  As a result, it became common for various teams and individual cricket players to promote various consumer goods which aided in its globalization.  === 21st century === Sachin Tendulkar was one of the key members during 1989–2013 for Team India in multiple formats.  Since 2000, the Indian team underwent major improvements with the appointment of John Wright, India's first ever foreign coach.  This appointment met success internationally as India maintained their unbeaten home record against Australia in Test series after defeating them in 2001 and won the inaugural ICC World Twenty20 in 2007.  India was also the first sub-continental team to win at the WACA in January 2008 against Australia"
    },
