      "answer": "Scheduled Caste",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Examples of crimes punishable under the Act include \"forcing victims to eat or drink obnoxious substances; dumping excreta, sewage, carcasses into their homes or compounds; land grabbing; humiliation; sexual abuse\".  The National Crime Records Bureau includes statistics of crimes reported under the law as part of it annual reports.  There has been a growth in total number of crimes reported under the Act in recent years but conviction rates have been low.  Crimes against members of Scheduled Caste communities grew by 7. 3% and against Scheduled Tribes by 26.  === Indian diaspora === Caste persists within the Indian diaspora.  In the United States, Dalit people report experiencing discrimination and violence"
