      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Group A jobs are senior most, high paying positions in the government, while Group D are junior most, lowest paying positions.  In Group D jobs, the percentage of positions held by lowest caste classified people is 30% greater than their demographic percentage.  In all jobs classified as Group C positions, the percentage of jobs held by lowest caste people is about the same as their demographic population distribution.  In Group A and B jobs, the percentage of positions held by lowest caste classified people is 30% lower than their demographic percentage.  The presence of lowest caste people in highest paying, senior-most position jobs in India has increased by ten-fold, from 1. 18 percent of all jobs in 1959 to 10. 12 percent of all jobs in 1995"
