      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:03:34.273Z",
      "subject": "Society",
      "subSubject": "Society",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "== Problems and Issues == === Facilities === As per the 2016 _____ of Education Report (ASER), 3",
      "answer": "Annual Survey",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === Vocational education === An optimistic estimate from 2008 was that only one in five job-seekers in India ever had any sort of vocational training.  However, it is expected to grow as the CBSE has brought changes in its education system which emphasises inclusion of certain number and types of vocational subjects in classes 9th and 11th.  Although it is not mandatory for schools to go for it but a good number of schools have voluntarily accepted the suggestion and incorporated the change in their curriculum.  == Problems and Issues == === Facilities === As per the 2016 Annual Survey of Education Report (ASER), 3. 5% schools in India had no toilet facility while only 68. 7% schools had usable toilet facility. 5% of the schools surveyed had a library in 2016, a decrease from 78"
    },
