      "fact": "98% while Rajasthan has the lowest female literacy rate of 52.  This correlates to the health levels of states, Kerala has average life expectancy at birth of 74. 9 while Rajasthan's average life expectancy at birth is 67.  In India, higher education is defined as the education of an age group between 18 and 24, and is largely funded by the government.  Despite women making up 24–50% of higher education enrolment, there is still a gender imbalance within higher education.  Only one third of science students and 7% of engineering students, are women.  In comparison, however, over half the students studying Education are women"
