      "answer": "In January",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Only one third of science students and 7% of engineering students, are women.  In comparison, however, over half the students studying Education are women.  === Accreditation === In 2018, 277 fake engineering colleges were identified.  In January 2010, the Government of India decided to withdraw Deemed university status from as many as 44 institutions.  The Government claimed in its affidavit that academic considerations were not being kept in mind by the management of these institutions and that \"they were being run as family fiefdoms\".  In February 2009, the University Grant Commission found 39 fake institutions operating in India.  === Employer training === Only 16% of manufacturers in India offer in-service training to their employees, compared with over 90% in China"
    },
