      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In 2024, that figure had dropped close to 10%, which triggered a debate of the skill gaps.  == Initiatives == === Central government involvement === Following India's independence, a number of rules were formulated for the backward Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes of India.  In 1960, a list identifying 405 Scheduled Castes and 225 Scheduled Tribes was published by the central government.  An amendment was made to the list in 1975, which identified 841 Scheduled Castes and 510 Scheduled Tribes.  The total percentage of Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes combined was found to be 22. 5% with the Scheduled Castes accounting for 17% and the Scheduled Tribes accounting for the remaining 7.  Following the report many Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes increasingly referred to themselves as Dalit, a Marathi language terminology used by B R Ambedkar which literally means \"oppressed\""
