      "question": "_____ poetry such as the Cilappadhikaram, describes women in exquisite drapery or sari",
      "answer": "Ancient Tamil",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " == Culture and heritage == === Clothing === Tamil women traditionally wear a sari, a garment measuring 15 to 27 ft (4. 2 m) in length and 2 to 4 ft (0. 22 m) in breadth that is typically wrapped around the waist, with one end draped over the shoulder, baring the midriff, as according to Indian philosophy, the navel is considered as the source of life and creativity.  Ancient Tamil poetry such as the Cilappadhikaram, describes women in exquisite drapery or sari.  Women wear colourful silk saris on special occasions such as marriages.  The Kanchipuram silk sari is a type of silk sari made in the Kanchipuram region in Tamil Nadu and these saris are worn as a part of the bridal attire and during special occasions.  It has been recognised as a Geographical indication by the Government of India in 2005–2006"
    },
