      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Tamil Lexicon, published by the University of Madras, is the first among the dictionaries published in any Indian language.  The 19th century gave rise to the Tamil Renaissance and writings and poems by authors such as Meenakshi Sundaram Pillai, U.  Swaminatha Iyer, Ramalinga Swamigal, Maraimalai Adigal, and Bharathidasan.  During the Indian Independence Movement, many Tamil poets and writers sought to provoke national spirit, social equity and secularist thoughts, notably Subramania Bharati and Bharathidasan.  === Architecture === Dravidian architecture is the distinct style of rock architecture in Tamil Nadu.  In Dravidian architecture, the temples consisted of porches or mantapas preceding the door leading to the sanctum, gate-pyramids or gopurams in quadrangular enclosures that surround the temple, and pillared halls used for many purposes.  These features are the invariable accompaniments of these temples"
