      "question": "A week after his 6 November 1924 arrival in _____, an ill Tagore shifted to the Villa Miralrío at the behest of Victoria Ocampo",
      "answer": "Buenos Aires",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Shortly after returning home, the 63-year-old Tagore accepted an invitation from the Peruvian government.  He travelled to Mexico.  Each government pledged US$100,000 to his school to commemorate the visits.  A week after his 6 November 1924 arrival in Buenos Aires, an ill Tagore shifted to the Villa Miralrío at the behest of Victoria Ocampo.  He left for home in January 1925.  In May 1926 Tagore reached Naples; the next day he met Mussolini in Rome.  Their warm rapport ended when Tagore felt compelled to denounce Fascism in an article published in The Manchester Guardian"
    },
