      "answer": "Lake Balaton",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " There is such a massive vigor in that head that it reminds one of Michael Angelo's chisel. \" A \"fire-bath\" of fascism was to have educed \"the immortal soul of Italy .  clothed in quenchless light\".  On 1 November 1926 Tagore arrived in Hungary and spent some time on the shore of Lake Balaton in the city of Balatonfüred, recovering from heart problems at a sanitarium.  He planted a tree, and a bust statue was placed there in 1956 (a gift from the Indian government, the work of Rasithan Kashar, replaced by a newly gifted statue in 2005) and the lakeside promenade still bears his name since 1957.  In 1927, Tagore travelled for four months to Southeast Asia, stopping in British Malaya, Siam and the Dutch East Indies.  Tagore was accompanied by the linguist Suniti Kumar Chatterji and visited the Buddhist shrine of Borobudur"
    },
