      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:04:13.146Z",
      "subject": "Books & Authors",
      "subSubject": "Books & Authors",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ was one of the greatest travelled scholars of India, spending forty-five years of his life on travels away from his home",
      "answer": "Rahul Sankrityayan",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " He was a noted satirist and humorist of modern Hindi literature and is known for his simple and direct style. , Sri Lal Sukla, Suryakumar Pandey etc.  === Hindi travel literature === Rahul Sankrityayan, Bhadant Anand Kausalyayan, Sachchidananda Hirananda Vatsyayan 'Ajneya' and Baba Nagarjun were some of the great Indian writers who dedicated themselves entirely to the Hindi Travel Literature (Yatra Vritanta).  Rahul Sankrityayan was one of the greatest travelled scholars of India, spending forty-five years of his life on travels away from his home.  He is known as the (\"Father of Hindi Travel literature\").  Baba Nagarjun was a major Hindi and Maithili poet who has also penned a number of novels, short stories, literary biographies and travelogues, and was known as (\"Janakavi- the People's Poet\").  === Hindi playwriting === The pioneer of Hindi theatre as well as playwrighting, Bhartendu Harishchandra wrote Satya Harishchandra (1875), Bharat Durdasha (1876) and Andher Nagari (1878), in the late 19th century, Jaishankar Prasad became the next big figure in Hindi playwriting with plays like Skanda Gupta (1928), Chandragupta (1931) and Dhruvswamini (1933)"
    },
