      "fact": "81 trillion (US$71 billion).  == Issues == === Corruption === In 2009, several ministers are accused of corruption and nearly a quarter of the 543 elected members of parliament had been charged with crimes, including murder.  Many of the biggest scandals since 2010 have involved high-level government officials, including cabinet ministers and chief ministers, such as the 2010 Commonwealth Games scandal (₹700 billion (equivalent to ₹1. 6 trillion or US$16 billion in 2023)), the Adarsh Housing Society scandal, the Coal allocation scandal (₹1. 86 trillion (equivalent to ₹4. 2 trillion or US$44 billion in 2023)), the mining scandal in Karnataka and the cash-for-votes scandal.  == See also == Foreign relations of India List of central agencies in India National Portal of India National Social-media Portal Union government ministries of India == References == == Further reading == Subrata K"
