      "answer": "Spice Group",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Micromax: 3 new manufacturing units in Rajasthan, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh with ₹3 billion (US$31 million) investment.  Qualcomm: \"Design in India\" programme to mentor ten Indian hardware companies with the potential to come up with innovative solutions and help them reach global scale.  Samsung: 10 \"MSME-Samsung Technical Schools\" and manufacturing of Samsung Z1 in its plant in Noida.  Spice Group: ₹5 billion (US$52 million) mobile phone manufacturing unit in Uttar Pradesh.  Vivo Mobile India began manufacturing smartphones at a plant in Greater Noida with 2,200 employees.  Wistron: Taiwanese company to start manufacturing of Blackberry, HTC and Motorola devices at a new factory in Noida.  Xiaomi: smartphones to be manufactured at a Foxconn-run facility in Sri City made operational by producing Xiaomi Redmi 2 Prime"
