      "fact": " == Branches and support bodies == The RBI has four regional representations: North in New Delhi, South in Chennai, East in Kolkata and West in Mumbai.  The representations are formed by five members, appointed for four years by the central government and with the advice of the central board of directors serve as a forum for regional banks and to deal with delegated tasks from the Central Board.  RBI has 31 branches in India.  Mostly all are in Capital cities, exceptions are the Kanpur, Nagpur and Ahmedabad Reserve Bank branches.  Kanpur office was established in 1935 as one of the five original branch offices, Nagpur office was established in 1956, while the Ahmedabad office was established in 1950.  It has 3 training colleges for its officers, viz.  Reserve Bank Staff College Chennai, Reserve Bank of India Academy Mumbai, and Reserve Bank of India College of Agricultural Banking Pune"
