      "question": "=== _____ === Payments bank is a new model of banks conceptualized by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI)",
      "answer": "Payment Banks",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "5 Crore (15 million) bank accounts were opened under this scheme. 2 million) accounts were opened, with around ₹20,288. 1 billion) were deposited under the scheme, which also has an option for opening new bank accounts with zero balance.  === Payment Banks === Payments bank is a new model of banks conceptualized by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI).  These banks can accept a restricted deposit, which is currently limited to ₹2 lakh per customer.  These banks may not issue loans or credit cards, but may offer both current and savings accounts.  Payments banks may issue ATM and debit cards, and offer net-banking and mobile-banking"
    },
